[23:45:20] [SUCCESS]   Level A: PASS — qualitative agreement reproduced
[23:45:20] [TEST]   --- Level B: Binned H_0(z) in Jia et al. bins ---
[23:45:20] [PROCESS] Methodology: Per-SN H0 is computed via standard LCDM inversion H0 = (1+z)*c*integral_0^z dz'/E(z') / d_L, where d_L = 10^((mu-25)/5) and E(z) = sqrt(Omega_m*(1+z)^3 + (1-Omega_m)) with Omega_m = 0.302. SNe are then binned into Jia et al.'s 10 equal-width bins (Table 4 edges) and the unweighted mean and standard error of the mean are computed per bin. This direct binned estimator is compared with Jia et al.'s published H_{0,z_i} values to assess whether the declining trend is present in the underlying observable or only in the reconstructed parameterization.
